From d050a269793317cb957794d00d0952a72024bba8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add JMH benchmarks used to evaluate the performance patches

MultiValuedDocValuesIterationBenchmark, PostingsEnumAllocationBenchmark,
SparsePointRangeQueryBenchmark, SparseFilterBulkScorerBenchmark and
DenseFilterBulkScorerBenchmark all go through IndexSearcher (or LeafReader for the
nextDoc variants), check in their setup that the implementation that they mean to
measure is the one that runs, and can keep their index in the directory given by
-Dbench.index.dir so that different builds of lucene-core can be compared on the
very same index.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
